endobj
105 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 65 0 R
/E (For those who may be new to my updates, I am back in Kisiizi, Uganda, serving as a nurse at Kisiizi Hospital. I work alongside Ugandan nurses, doctors, students, and other staff, caring for patients primarily on the paediatric and medical wards. My days also include teaching, small research and quality-improvement projects, hospital communications, and plenty of opportunities to become involved in the life of the community beyond the hospital walls.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
106 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 65 0 R
/E (I first came to Kisiizi for a shorter season of service, but somewhere along the way, this little mountain community began to feel like home. After my second visit, I sensed God leading me back for something longer. So, in June, I returned to begin a three-year season of volunteer service.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
107 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 65 0 R
/E (I knew coming back would bring challenges. I expected the long days, the unfamiliar cases, the language learning, and the occasional goat-related inconvenience. What I didn't quite anticipate was how often I would be reminded that what I have is not always enough.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
108 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 65 0 R
/E (Because here, as in so many places, the need is often greater than what we have to give.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
