<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 66 0 R
/E (But being known as a place that will help also comes with its own challenges. The hospital has limited resources, and the needs are certainly not limited. There are patients who genuinely cannot afford everything they need, and there are also times when people who could contribute toward their care know that Kisiizi is unlikely to simply turn them away. It can make decisions about financial assistance complicated.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
123 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 66 0 R
/E (How do you remain generous without making promises you cannot keep? How do you steward what has been entrusted to the hospital when you know there will always be another person waiting who needs help?)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
124 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 66 0 R
/E (These are not abstract questions here. They are part of everyday hospital life.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
125 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 66 0 R
/E (Sometimes the limitation is money. Sometimes it is equipment. Sometimes it is time or staff. Sometimes you are working through a clinical problem and the option you would normally reach for simply isn't available. You look at what you have and realize that it isn't everything you would like to have.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
126 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 66 0 R
/E (And I have found myself thinking about that phrase quite a lot since coming back: It isn't enough.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
