167 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 69 0 R
/E (There is a little boy in our nursery named Blessing who has become a regular part of my days. He is nearly four months old, and his story is difficult to imagine. Shortly after he was born, he was found abandoned by a Good Samaritan. Against all odds, he survived and was brought to Kisiizi. The medical team struggled to provide all the care he needed. He was so sick when he arrived that many doubted he would survive a few days, much less a few months. He needed strong antibiotics, platelet transfusions, and constant monitoring.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
168 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 69 0 R
/E (His circumstances remain complicated, and there are still many unanswered questions about his family and what his future will look like. But for now, he is safe, growing, and very much loved by the people caring for him.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
169 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 69 0 R
/E (He has also become a regular companion on my days and nights after clinical work. Some days he comes home with me, where he eats, sleeps, gets cuddled, and generally takes over the house. I have to admit, I am quite happy to let him.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
170 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 69 0 R
/E (His story could have ended very differently. I am grateful it didn't.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [10]
>>
